/*Q10. Write a Java program that prompts the user to enter a string and a character. If the character is present in the string, print the index of the
character; otherwise, print "Not found".
Input Format:
• The first line is a string of multiple characters (alphabets, digits, special characters).
• The second line is a single character.
Output Format:
• If the character is present in the string, the output is the integer that represents the index of the character in the string; otherwise, it
displays "Not found."
Note: If the character occurs multiple times in the string, the index of its first occurrence should be printed.*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class CharIndex {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        char ch = sc.nextLine().charAt(0);
        int idx = s.indexOf(ch);           // first occurrence
        if (idx != -1) System.out.println(idx);
        else System.out.println("Not found");
        sc.close();
    }
}
